{"name":"Tassel Flower","hex":"#f9c0ce","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tassel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A ball-shaped bunch of plaited or otherwise entangled threads from which at one end protrudes a cord on which the ball is hung, and which may have loose, dangling threads at the other end (often used as decoration along the bottom of garments, curtains or other hangings).","The panicle on a male plant of maize, which consists of loose threads with anthers on them."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To adorn with tassels.","To put forth a tassel or flower."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tassel"},{"term":"flower","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colorful, conspicuous structure associated with angiosperms, frequently scented and attracting various insects, and which may or may not be used for sexual reproduction.","A reproductive structure in angiosperms (flowering plants), often conspicuously colourful and typically including sepals, petals, and either or both stamens and/or a pistil."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To put forth blooms.","To decorate with pictures of flowers."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flower"}],"entries":[{"title":"Emilia (plant)","blocks":[{"text":"Emilia is a genus of herbaceous plants in the sunflower family, known as tasselflower or pualele."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Starr_050405-5699_Emilia_fosbergii.jpg/330px-Starr_050405-5699_Emilia_fosbergii.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emilia_(plant)"},{"title":"Tassel","blocks":[{"text":"A tassel is a finishing feature in fabric and clothing decoration. It is a universal ornament that is seen in varying versions in many cultures around the globe."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Tassel2.svg/330px-Tassel2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tassel"},{"title":"Flower","blocks":[{"text":"Flowers, also known as blossoms and blooms, are the reproductive structures of flowering plants. Typically, they are structured in four circular levels around the end of a stalk. These include: sepals, which are modified leaves that support the flower; petals, often designed to attract pollinators; male stamens, where pollen is presented; and female gynoecia, where pollen is received and its movement is facilitated to the egg. When flowers are arranged in a group, they are known collectively as an inflorescence."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Magnolia_grandiflora_-_flower_1.jpg/330px-Magnolia_grandiflora_-_flower_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flower"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Orna118-Quasten.png/500px-Orna118-Quasten.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Orna118-Quasten.png/500px-Orna118-Quasten.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Illustration of various tassels, from A Handbook of Ornament, by Franz Sales Meyer","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOrna118-Quasten.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Tester_bed_%28lit_%C3%A0_la_duchesse_en_imp%C3%A9riale%29_MET_DP155162.jpg/500px-Tester_bed_%28lit_%C3%A0_la_duchesse_en_imp%C3%A9riale%29_MET_DP155162.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Tester_bed_%28lit_%C3%A0_la_duchesse_en_imp%C3%A9riale%29_MET_DP155162.jpg/1280px-Tester_bed_%28lit_%C3%A0_la_duchesse_en_imp%C3%A9riale%29_MET_DP155162.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&u